{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"1174","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"B. Ehab Is an Odd Person"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"1 second"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You're given an array $$$a$$$ of length $$$n$$$. You can perform the following operation on it as many times as you want:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" Pick two integers $$$i$$$ and $$$j$$$ $$$(1 \\le i,j \\le n)$$$ such that "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"$$$a_i+a_j$$$ is odd"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":", then swap $$$a_i$$$ and $$$a_j$$$. "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"What is lexicographically the smallest array you can obtain?"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"An array $$$x$$$ is "},{"attrs":{"href":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lexicographical_order"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"lexicographically smaller"}],"kind":"link"},{"kind":"text","text":" than an array $$$y$$$ if there exists an index $$$i$$$ such that $$$x_i \\lt y_i$$$, and $$$x_j=y_j$$$ for all $$$1 \\le j \\lt i$$$. Less formally, at the first index $$$i$$$ in which they differ, $$$x_i \\lt y_i$$$"}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line contains an integer $$$n$$$ ($$$1 \\le n \\le 10^5$$$) — the number of elements in the array $$$a$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The second line contains $$$n$$$ space-separated integers $$$a_1$$$, $$$a_2$$$, $$$\\ldots$$$, $$$a_{n}$$$ ($$$1 \\le a_i \\le 10^9$$$) — the elements of the array $$$a$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The only line contains $$$n$$$ space-separated integers, the lexicographically smallest array you can obtain."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Examples"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n3\n4 1 7\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n1 4 7 "}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n2\n1 1\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n1 1 "}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the first example, we can swap $$$1$$$ and $$$4$$$ since $$$1+4=5$$$, which is odd."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"docume